  "status_text": "The shared-gate question now has a checked answer in its smallest case: no circuit of at most 5 AND, OR and NOT gates of fan-in at most two computes both a1 b1 or a2 b2 and a1 c1 or a2 c2, so these two outputs cannot share a gate to save one, even with NOT gates. Seats found the argument by hand this afternoon; a contributor's Lean proof was checked at 18:45. Next under attack: the same question for four outputs at once. Small cases are a table, not a law.",
